  'What are the three elements of self-defense?',
  '[{"text":"Unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity, lack of sufficient provocation","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"rationale":"The three elements are: unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity of the means employed, and lack of sufficient provocation on the part of the person defending himself."},{"text":"Intent, motive, opportunity","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"rationale":"''Intent, motive, opportunity'' is incorrect. The correct answer is ''Unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity, lack of sufficient provocation''. The three elements are: unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity of the means employed, and lack of sufficient provocation on the part of the person defending himself. Review: Justifying Circumstances."},{"text":"Premeditation, treachery, evident premeditation","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"rationale":"''Premeditation, treachery, evident premeditation'' is incorrect. The correct answer is ''Unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity, lack of sufficient provocation''. The three elements are: unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity of the means employed, and lack of sufficient provocation on the part of the person defending himself. Review: Justifying Circumstances."},{"text":"Minority, insanity, imbecility","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"rationale":"''Minority, insanity, imbecility'' is incorrect. The correct answer is ''Unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity, lack of sufficient provocation''. The three elements are: unlawful aggression, reasonable necessity of the means employed, and lack of sufficient provocation on the part of the person defending himself. Review: Justifying Circumstances."}]'::jsonb,
