  'qb_cj_006',
  'criminal_jurisprudence',
  'Rules of Court',
  'A warrantless arrest is valid when:',
  '[{"text":"The person is suspected of any crime","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"rationale":"''The person is suspected of any crime'' is incorrect. The correct answer is ''The person is committing, has just committed, or is about to commit a crime in the presence of the arresting officer''. Under Rule 113, Section 5, warrantless arrests are valid for in flagrante delicto, hot pursuit, and escaped prisoners. Review: Rules of Court."},{"text":"The person is committing, has just committed, or is about to commit a crime in the presence of the arresting officer","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"rationale":"Under Rule 113, Section 5, warrantless arrests are valid for in flagrante delicto, hot pursuit, and escaped prisoners."},{"text":"The arresting officer has a personal grudge","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"rationale":"''The arresting officer has a personal grudge'' is incorrect. The correct answer is ''The person is committing, has just committed, or is about to commit a crime in the presence of the arresting officer''. Under Rule 113, Section 5, warrantless arrests are valid for in flagrante delicto, hot pursuit, and escaped prisoners. Review: Rules of Court."},{"text":"The crime was committed last month","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"rationale":"''The crime was committed last month'' is incorrect. The correct answer is ''The person is committing, has just committed, or is about to commit a crime in the presence of the arresting officer''. Under Rule 113, Section 5, warrantless arrests are valid for in flagrante delicto, hot pursuit, and escaped prisoners. Review: Rules of Court."}]'::jsonb,
